f main() int{
    return crossTable(true)
}

/*
    -- TODO! --
    this code currently will not compile, as cross matching is yet to be implemented.

    Q4r doesn't have a default `switch` statement,
    it actually mounts something I call a `cross` table.

    `cross` tables are basically jump tables used to match the pattern
    of different values.

    ```quaoar
    cross value{
        1: return 1,
        2: return 2,
        3: return 3,
        // ...
    }
    ```
*/
f crossTable(bool value) int{
    cross value{
        true: return 0,
        false: return 1
    }
}